# Design + motion system

Do not design while coding. Order: **creative direction → spec → implement → responsive/motion/a11y review**.

This repo: **Vite + React + Tailwind + Motion**. Tailwind is layout/tokens. Motion is animation. shadcn/Aceternity/Tailwind UI are research only — never the visual identity. Do not add Next.js. GSAP / Lenis / Three.js only if the concept cannot be done in Motion and you can justify it.

## Creative direction (write in SPEC.md first)

Pick one style (Editorial / Brutalist / Futuristic / Luxury / Playful). Define type, layout, color, motion, and a **signature motif**. Five components in a batch must not share the same signature.

## Design rules

1. No generic SaaS landing pages or identical card grids.
2. Strong visual concept before components. Asymmetry and oversized type are design tools; whitespace is intentional.
3. Every stage has a clear hierarchy. Prefer composition over decoration.
4. Motion communicates hierarchy or interaction — never motion for its own sake.
5. Touch-first: hover is optional enhancement, never required to understand content.
6. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Design mobile independently (not a compressed desktop).
7. Reuse **tokens and motion primitives**, not the same section look twice.

## Motion language (`src/lib/motion.ts`)

| Role | Duration |
|------|----------|
| Micro | 150–250ms |
| Standard | 300–500ms |
| Emphasis | 600–1000ms |
| Hero | 1000–1500ms |

Named moves only: fade-up, fade-in, scale-in, slide-in, image-reveal, text-reveal, stagger, parallax, magnetic, marquee. Hero = highly animated; primary interaction = noticeable; content = subtle; chrome = restrained.

## Responsive (mobile → tablet → desktop → large)

Each SPEC must define layout, type scale, spacing, image crop, interaction, and animation **per breakpoint**. Desktop may use hover / mouse-follow; mobile must not depend on them and should reduce motion.

## Tokens

Use `--duration-*`, `--text-display`, `--radius-*` from `src/index.css`. Change personality via tokens, not one-off magic numbers.
